From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:32:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 071/154] feat(core): expose the routing decision across the
 ABI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Takes routing.json's contents rather than reading it, because the store layer
here has never done file IO and the caller already loads the file once at wiring
time. Parsing per call is affordable: navigations happen at human speed and the
file holds a handful of rules.

Null is "no rule claims this url" and also every failure - unreadable input, a
file that does not parse, a schema this build refuses. The same answer on
purpose: routing is an enhancement, so a caller that cannot tell them apart
still does the right thing, which is to open the url where it was already going.

regex_lite needed its visibility widened. The generated BUILD.gn says how - add
the crate to chromium_crates_io - but that regenerates every crate target for one
dependency. The narrow version is recorded in gnrt_config.toml as well as in the
generated file, so a later regen reproduces it rather than dropping it.

Also fixes drift this bump uncovered: atrium_core_sidebar_width reached the
header and the crate at ABI 35 and never reached the pinned export list, so that
test had been failing since. Third time this has happened on a bump.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml | 3 +++
 third_party/rust/regex_lite/v0_1/BUILD.gn            | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml
index 9ae14f802aff7..8561d000ac2a3 100644
--- a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml
+++ b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml
@@ -745,6 +745,9 @@ allow_unsafe = true
 
 [crate.regex-lite]
 extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = false }
+# Atrium's core matches routing rules with this. The wildcard is the default
+# this list replaces, so it has to be repeated rather than added to.
+visibility = ['//third_party/rust/*', '//third_party/atrium/core:*']
 
 [crate.regex-syntax.extra_kv]
 allow_unsafe = false
diff --git a/third_party/rust/regex_lite/v0_1/BUILD.gn b/third_party/rust/regex_lite/v0_1/BUILD.gn
index ce25fea76942c..09d284b0f6030 100644
--- a/third_party/rust/regex_lite/v0_1/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/rust/regex_lite/v0_1/BUILD.gn
@@ -49,7 +49,10 @@ cargo_crate("lib") {
   # Only for usage from third-party crates. Add the crate to
   # //third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/Cargo.toml to use
   # it from first-party code.
-  visibility = [ "//third_party/rust/*" ]
+  visibility = [
+    "//third_party/rust/*",
+    "//third_party/atrium/core:*",
+  ]
 
   #####################################################################
   # Tweaking which GN `config`s apply to this target.
